{
  "openapi": "3.1.1",
  "info": {
    "title": "Mutations API",
    "version": "v2025-02-19",
    "description": "The Mutations API lets you create, update, and delete documents in Sanity Content Lake.\n\n### Transactions\nThe mutation API is transactional. \nYou may submit an array of mutations and if the operation succeeds you can rest assured that every mutation you submitted was executed.\n\n### Mutation Types\n\nThe API supports several types of mutations:\n- create: Creates a new document with a specified or generated ID\n- createOrReplace: Creates a new document or replaces an existing one\n- createIfNotExists: Creates a document only if it doesn't already exist\n- delete: Removes documents by ID or GROQ query\n- patch: Updates existing documents with various operations\n\n#### Create Mutation\nCreates a new document. The rules for the new document's identifier are:\n- If _id is missing, a new random unique ID is generated\n- If _id ends with '.', it is used as a prefix for a new random unique ID\n- If _id is present, it is used as-is\n\nThe operation will fail if a document by the provided ID already exists.\n\n#### CreateOrReplace Mutation\nCreates a new document or replaces an existing one. If the document already exists:\n- If the type is the same, the document will be completely replaced\n- If the type is different, it will act as a delete then create\n- If the document has hard references pointing to it, changing its type is not allowed\n\n#### CreateIfNotExists Mutation\nCreates a new document, but will silently fail if the document already exists.\nOtherwise identical to create mutation.\n\n#### Delete Mutation\nDeletes a document. Can delete by ID or by GROQ query.\nThe operation is considered successful even if the document did not exist.\n\nWhen using a query to delete multiple documents:\n- The query can only operate on up to 10,000 documents\n- For larger sets, split into multiple transactions\n- Recommended to paginate by _id using queries like `*[_type == \"article\" && _id > $lastId]`\n\n#### Patch Mutation\nUpdates an existing document's contents. A patch will fail if the document does not exist.\nCan patch by ID or by GROQ query.\n\nIf multiple patches are included, the order of execution is:\n\n1. set\n2. setIfMissing\n3. unset\n4. inc\n5. dec\n6. insert\n\nLearn more about the patches [here](https://www.sanity.io/docs/http-patches).\n\nNote: While you can use the HTTP API endpoint directly, we recommend using a client library if you can.\n"
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://{projectId}.api.sanity.io/{apiVersion}",
      "description": "Sanity API base URL",
      "variables": {
        "projectId": {
          "default": "projectId",
          "description": "Project ID"
        },
        "apiVersion": {
          "default": "v2025-02-19",
          "description": "API version"
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "security": [
    {
      "BearerAuth": []
    }
  ],
  "paths": {
    "/data/mutate/{dataset}": {
      "post": {
        "summary": "Mutate documents",
        "description": "Create, update, or delete documents in your dataset.\n",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "dataset",
            "in": "path",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "description": "The dataset to mutate"
          },
          {
            "name": "returnIds",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "type": "boolean",
              "default": false
            },
            "description": "If true, the id's of modified documents are returned."
          },
          {
            "name": "returnDocuments",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "type": "boolean",
              "default": false
            },
            "description": "If true, the entire content of changed documents is returned."
          },
          {
            "name": "autoGenerateArrayKeys",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "type": "boolean",
              "default": false
            },
            "description": "If true, adds a _key attribute to array items, unique within the array, to ensure each can be addressed uniquely in a real-time collaboration context, even if elements are inserted or removed elsewhere in the array."
          },
          {
            "name": "transactionId",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "description": "By default every transaction gets a random ID. This is included in Listener mutation events and the History API. This parameter lets you set your own transaction ID. It must be unique in the dataset."
          },
          {
            "name": "skipCrossDatasetReferencesValidation",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "type": "boolean",
              "default": false
            },
            "description": "If true then any cross-dataset references will be considered weak for the purposes of this mutation."
          },
          {
            "name": "visibility",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "default": "sync"
            },
            "description": "Can be: sync, async or deferred If sync the request will not return until the requested changes are visible to subsequent queries, if async the request will return immediately when the changes have been committed, but it might still be a second or so until you can see the change reflected in a query. For maximum performance, use async always, except when you need your next query to see the changes you made. deferred is the fastest way to write. It bypasses the real time indexing completely, and should be used in cases where you are bulk importing/mutating a large number of documents and don't need to see that data in a query for several tens of seconds.\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "dryRun",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "type": "boolean"
            },
            "description": "If true, the mutation will be validated but not executed"
          },
          {
            "name": "tag",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "description": "Request tags are values assigned to API and CDN requests that can be used to filter and aggregate log data within \n[request logs from your Sanity Content Lake](https://www.sanity.io/docs/platform-management/request-logs). Learn more in the [request tags documentation](https://www.sanity.io/docs/platform-management/reference-api-request-tags).\n"
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/MutationRequest"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successful mutation",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/MutationResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Invalid request"
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Unauthorized"
          },
          "403": {
            "description": "Forbidden"
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Dataset not found"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "components": {
    "securitySchemes": {
      "BearerAuth": {
        "type": "http",
        "scheme": "bearer",
        "description": "Bearer token authentication"
      }
    },
    "schemas": {
      "MutationRequest": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "mutations"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "mutations": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Mutation"
            },
            "description": "Array of mutations to perform"
          }
        },
        "example": {
          "mutations": [
            {
              "create": {
                "_id": "123",
                "_type": "cms.article",
                "title": "An article"
              }
            },
            {
              "createOrReplace": {
                "_id": "456",
                "_type": "cms.article",
                "title": "Another article"
              }
            },
            {
              "delete": {
                "id": "789"
              }
            },
            {
              "patch": {
                "id": "123",
                "set": {
                  "title": "Updated title"
                },
                "inc": {
                  "viewCount": 1
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "MutationResponse": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "transactionId": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Unique identifier for the transaction"
          },
          "results": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/MutationResult"
            },
            "description": "Results of each mutation"
          }
        },
        "example": {
          "transactionId": "txn_123456",
          "results": [
            {
              "operation": "create",
              "documentId": "123"
            },
            {
              "operation": "createOrReplace",
              "documentId": "456"
            },
            {
              "operation": "delete",
              "documentId": "789"
            },
            {
              "operation": "patch",
              "documentId": "123"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "MutationResult": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "operation": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The type of mutation performed"
          },
          "documentId": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The ID of the affected document"
          }
        }
      },
      "Mutation": {
        "type": "object",
        "oneOf": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CreateMutation"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CreateOrReplaceMutation"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CreateIfNotExistsMutation"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/DeleteMutation"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/PatchMutation"
          }
        ]
      },
      "CreateMutation": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "create"
        ],
        "description": "Creates a new document. The rules for the new document's identifier are:\n- If _id is missing, a new random unique ID is generated\n- If _id ends with '.', it is used as a prefix for a new random unique ID\n- If _id is present, it is used as-is\n\nThe operation will fail if a document by the provided ID already exists.\n",
        "properties": {
          "create": {
            "type": "object",
            "description": "Document to create",
            "required": [
              "_type"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "_id": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Document ID. Can be:\n- Omitted to generate a random ID\n- A string ending with '.' to use as prefix for random ID\n- A specific ID to use as-is\n"
              },
              "_type": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Document type name"
              },
              "_createdAt": {
                "type": "string",
                "format": "date-time",
                "description": "Creation timestamp. If omitted, current time is used"
              },
              "_updatedAt": {
                "type": "string",
                "format": "date-time",
                "description": "Last update timestamp. If omitted, current time is used"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "example": {
          "create": {
            "_id": "123",
            "_type": "cms.article",
            "title": "An article"
          }
        }
      },
      "CreateOrReplaceMutation": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "createOrReplace"
        ],
        "description": "Creates a new document or replaces an existing one. If the document already exists:\n- If the type is the same, the document will be completely replaced\n- If the type is different, it will act as a delete then create\n- If the document has hard references pointing to it, changing its type is not allowed\n",
        "properties": {
          "createOrReplace": {
            "type": "object",
            "description": "Document to create or replace",
            "required": [
              "_type"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "_id": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Document ID"
              },
              "_type": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Document type name"
              },
              "_createdAt": {
                "type": "string",
                "format": "date-time",
                "description": "Creation timestamp. If omitted, current time is used"
              },
              "_updatedAt": {
                "type": "string",
                "format": "date-time",
                "description": "Last update timestamp. If omitted, current time is used"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "example": {
          "createOrReplace": {
            "_id": "456",
            "_type": "cms.article",
            "title": "Another article"
          }
        }
      },
      "CreateIfNotExistsMutation": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "createIfNotExists"
        ],
        "description": "Creates a new document, but will silently fail if the document already exists.\nOtherwise identical to create mutation.\n",
        "properties": {
          "createIfNotExists": {
            "type": "object",
            "description": "Document to create if it doesn't exist",
            "required": [
              "_type"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "_id": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Document ID"
              },
              "_type": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Document type name"
              },
              "_createdAt": {
                "type": "string",
                "format": "date-time",
                "description": "Creation timestamp. If omitted, current time is used"
              },
              "_updatedAt": {
                "type": "string",
                "format": "date-time",
                "description": "Last update timestamp. If omitted, current time is used"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "example": {
          "createIfNotExists": {
            "_id": "789",
            "_type": "cms.article",
            "title": "A new article"
          }
        }
      },
      "DeleteMutation": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "delete"
        ],
        "description": "Deletes a document. Can delete by ID or by GROQ query.\nThe operation is considered successful even if the document did not exist.\n\nWhen using a query to delete multiple documents:\n- The query can only operate on up to 10,000 documents\n- For larger sets, split into multiple transactions\n- Recommended to paginate by _id using queries like '*[_type == \"article\" && _id > $lastId]'\n- Deleting system documents requires \"manage\" permission.\n",
        "properties": {
          "delete": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "id"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "id": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "ID of document to delete"
              },
              "query": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "GROQ query to select documents to delete.\nExample: '*[_type == \"feature\" && viewCount < $views]'\n"
              },
              "params": {
                "type": "object",
                "description": "Parameters for the GROQ query"
              },
              "ifRevisionID": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Revision ID for optimistic locking.\nIf the document's current revision ID doesn't match,\nthe delete will fail. This can be used for optimistic locking, to make sure that mutations are applied in the exact order expected by the application.\n"
              },
              "purge": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "description": "If true, fully purges the document from transaction history.\nAll transactions related to the document will be immediately removed,\nconsistent with data retention policy.\nPurging requires the editHistory permission on the document, in addition to the permissions a regular delete needs. None of the predefined roles grant editHistory, including Administrator, so a purge request from an Administrator user or token fails with a 403 error: Insufficient permissions; permission \"editHistory\" required.\n"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "delete": {
              "id": "123"
            }
          },
          {
            "delete": {
              "query": "*[_type == 'feature' && viewCount < $views]",
              "params": {
                "views": 5
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "delete": {
              "id": "123",
              "purge": true
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "PatchMutation": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "patch"
        ],
        "description": "Updates an existing document's contents. A patch will fail if the document does not exist.\nCan patch by ID or by GROQ query.\n\nIf multiple patches are included, the order of execution is:\n1. set\n2. setIfMissing\n3. unset\n4. inc\n5. dec\n6. insert\n",
        "properties": {
          "patch": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "id"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "id": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "ID of document to patch"
              },
              "query": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "GROQ query to select documents to patch.\nExample: '*[_type == \"person\" && points >= $threshold]'\n"
              },
              "params": {
                "type": "object",
                "description": "Parameters for the GROQ query"
              },
              "ifRevisionID": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Revision ID for optimistic locking.\nIf the document's current revision ID doesn't match,\nthe patch will fail. This can be used for optimistic locking, to make sure that mutations are applied in the exact order expected by the application.\n"
              },
              "set": {
                "type": "object",
                "description": "Fields to set"
              },
              "setIfMissing": {
                "type": "object",
                "description": "Fields to set if they don't exist"
              },
              "unset": {
                "type": "array",
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "description": "Fields to remove"
              },
              "inc": {
                "type": "object",
                "description": "Fields to increment"
              },
              "dec": {
                "type": "object",
                "description": "Fields to decrement"
              },
              "insert": {
                "type": "object",
                "description": "Array insert operations"
              },
              "diffMatchPatch": {
                "type": "object",
                "description": "Text diff operations"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "patch": {
              "id": "123",
              "set": {
                "title": "Updated title"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "patch": {
              "id": "123",
              "ifRevisionID": "rev_123",
              "set": {
                "title": "Updated title"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "patch": {
              "id": "123",
              "set": {
                "title": "New title"
              },
              "setIfMissing": {
                "author": "John Doe"
              },
              "inc": {
                "viewCount": 1
              },
              "unset": [
                "oldField",
                "deprecatedField"
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "patch": {
              "query": "*[_type == 'person' && points >= $threshold]",
              "params": {
                "threshold": 100
              },
              "dec": {
                "points": 100
              },
              "inc": {
                "bonuses": 1
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}